## Why FAIL

The user's verification item 1 explicitly requires the wrapper to
contain "Mobile classes for edge-to-edge with white/blur
(`bg-white/95 backdrop-blur` or equivalent, plus `border-b`)" and
"md+ classes for rounded-2xl card with blue tint (`md:rounded-2xl`,
`md:border md:border-blue-100`, `md:bg-blue-50/80` or similar)".

The actual wrapper className is:
```
sticky top-0 z-10 -mx-4 md:mx-0
```

It contains NONE of the prescribed visual classes. The desktop
appearance is approximated by the pre-existing inner div's
`rounded-2xl border border-blue-200 bg-blue-50` styling, but:

- Mobile: there is no `bg-white/95`, no `backdrop-blur`, no
  `border-b`. The mobile AC "Banner edge-to-edge with white/blur
  background" is not met. As the teacher scrolls on a 375 × 667
  viewport, the inner blue card sticks at top with `-mx-4` breakout
  but no white/blur scrim covers content scrolling beneath it.
- Desktop: visually close to spec, but achieved by accident of the
  inner div, not by the wrapper className as the refined ticket
  prescribes.

This is a P2 visual bug — sticky positioning DOES fire and the
functional behavior is intact, but the prescribed mobile treatment
is missing.

